name: sim.setShapeMassAndInertia
description: 
luaSynopsis: sim.setShapeMassAndInertia(int shapeHandle,float mass,float[9] inertiaMatrix,float[3] centerOfMass,float[12] transformation=nil)
inputs (possibly taken/adapted from C-function counterpart. Adjust accordingly):
1. shapeHandle: handle of the shape object
2. mass: the new mass of the object
3. inertia matrix: the new inertia matrix (9 values), expressed relative to the center of mass. The matrix should be relative to the orientational frame of transformation (see further below).
4. centerOfMass: the new position of the center of mass, relative to the specified transformation (see next item).
5. transformation: the transformation matrix (12 values) relative to which we specify the data. Can be nullptr, in which case the data is relative to the absolute reference frame. See here to see how matrix transformations are specified in CoppeliaSim.
outputs (possibly taken/adapted from C-function counterpart. Adjust accordingly):
